cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, data or results, please cite this repository as below.
  The citation for the accompanying article will be added on publication.
title: "Bus Sathi: open-data bus route rationalisation and fleet sizing for Kashmir Division"
abstract: >-
  Code, data and results for an open-data, demand-free framework for bus route
  rationalisation and fleet sizing, applied to the ten districts of Kashmir Division,
  India (6.58 million residents). Includes the route-rationalisation engine and its
  published plan (186 routes, 1,011 buses), a driver-GPS ground-truth pipeline, and a
  23-module analysis that reproduces every result reported in the manuscript
  "Planning What You Cannot Count", including network walk catchments, six validation
  channels and a Monte Carlo / Sobol' uncertainty analysis.
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-30
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/Princu-Babu/Bus-sathi"
keywords:
  - public transport
  - bus route rationalisation
  - fleet sizing
  - open data
  - demand-data scarcity
  - walking catchments
  - uncertainty analysis
  - Kashmir
